<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Go-Komatsu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1377–1433</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Go-Komatsu was the sixth and last emperor of the Northern Court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and the 100th emperor in the traditional count, reigning from 1382 to 1412. In 1392 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-yoshimitsu">Ashikaga Yoshimitsu</a> arranged the return of the imperial regalia by the Southern emperor Go-Kameyama, ending the schism and making Go-Komatsu sole emperor. The promise to alternate the throne with the Southern line was not kept, and his son Shōkō succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-go-komatsu.jpg" alt="Emperor Go-Komatsu" width="320" height="275" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Go-Komatsu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
